[9.96169, "o", "\r\nLIVELOCK / STARVATION ISSUES DETECTED:"]
[9.962101, "o", "\r\n\r\nStarved Threads (never get CPU time):\r\n  - Finalizer\r\n\r\nThreads with No Progress:\r\n  - Reference Handler\r\n  - surefire-forkedjvm-command-thread\r\n  - HttpClient-1-SelectorManager\r\n  - Common-Cleaner\r\n  - surefire-forkedjvm-stream-flusher\r\n  - Signal Dispatcher\r\n  - Finalizer\r\n  - Notification Thread\r\n\r\nWhy: Starved threads are permanently blocked or never scheduled because other threads monopolize CPU or locks, causing tasks to silently stall or never execute. Threads with no progress are neither completing work nor making forward state changes — a sign of an unnoticed block or incorrect loop condition. \r\nFix:\r\n  - Livelock: introduce randomised back-off between retries — e.g. Thread.sleep(ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextInt(10, 50)) — so threads yield to each other rather than thrashing in lock-step\r\n  - Starvation: use a fair lock (new ReentrantLock(true)) so threads acquire in arrival order; reduce lock hold time; avoid priority inversion\r\n"]
[9.96224, "o", "  - No-progress threads: check for missed notify() calls, broken loop exit conditions, or tasks submitted to a saturated executor\r\n"]
[9.963056, "o", "\r\n"]
[9.963211, "o", "SHARED COLLECTION ISSUES DETECTED:"]
[9.963246, "o", "\r\n"]
[9.963271, "o", "  Concurrent Write Violations (data corruption risk):"]
[9.96337, "o", "\r\n    - request-log (ArrayList): write operations from 18 threads (writes: 18) — DATA CORRUPTION RISK!\r\n  Collection Activity:\r\n"]
[9.963752, "o", "    - request-log: reads: 0 from 0 thread(s), writes: 18 from 18 thread(s)\r\n  Why: ArrayList, HashMap, and similar collections are explicitly not thread-safe. Concurrent writes corrupt\r\n       internal array pointers and size counters, causing ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException, infinite loops inside\r\n       HashMap.get(), or silently lost entries — bugs that appear non-deterministically and are hard to reproduce.\r\n  Fix:\r\n    - Drop-in concurrent replacements: ConcurrentHashMap, ConcurrentLinkedQueue, CopyOnWriteArrayList\r\n    - Wrapper (coarse-grained): Collections.synchronizedList/Map/Set — remember to lock the collection during iteration\r\n    - Thread-confined: only access the collection from one thread; pass results between threads via a queue\r\n"]
[9.964886, "o", "\r\n\u001b[34m🟢 LOW\u001b[0m: Uncommitted repository changes detected\r\nImpact: Minor inefficiencies or best practice violations\r\n  Uncommitted files (modified/added/deleted):\r\n    - docs/diagrams/demo.cast [M]\r\n    - tools/demo/pom.xml [M]\r\n  Recommended fix: git add and git commit your changes to ensure a clean test baseline.\r\n"]
